<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:local="using:PhotoBook.Shell.Views"
             xmlns:controls="using:PhotoBook.Shell.Controls"
             x:Class="PhotoBook.Shell.Views.ProjectListView">

    <!--
        Two steps up on this screen, and only this screen.

        A project name is the one thing on this screen a person scans for from across the
        room, and sixteen pixels is not enough weight to be found. It goes to seventeen and
        stays bold. The body - the panel's subtitle, the counts under the rule, the call to
        action - goes to thirteen.

        Written here rather than in Typography.axaml: a twelve-pixel body is right in a
        dialog where the words are two lines long, and a scale that moves for one screen
        stops being a scale. These rules sit closer to their controls than the shared ones do,
        so they win on this screen only.

        The badge stays where it is. It is a label rather than a sentence, and at thirteen it
        would be the loudest thing on a card that has a name, a row of photographs and a
        button on it.
    -->
    <UserControl.Styles>
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.t12">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="13" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="TextBlock.t16Bold">
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="17" />
        </Style>

        <!--
            The stack of pages answers the pointer, the way the prototype's does: the front
            photograph rises ten pixels over half a second, and the two behind it keep still.
            Ten pixels is a photograph being picked up - more is a card trick.
        -->
        <Style Selector="Border.waFront">
            <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="rotate(-2deg)" />
        </Style>

        <Style Selector="Panel.welcomePanel:pointerover Border.waFront">
            <Setter Property="RenderTransform" Value="translate(0px,-10px) rotate(-2deg)" />
        </Style>

        <!--
            "Как это работает" is the second large button of the panel and it is a ghost:
            muted words, no box, and the box appears only under the pointer, at four and a
            half percent. Written out because the platform's button template paints its own
            wash and frame, which is a different control from this one.
        -->
        <Style Selector="Button.welcomeGhost">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="CornerRadius" Value="999" />
            <Setter Property="Height" Value="46" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="24,0" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="14" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextMuted}" />
            <Setter Property="Cursor" Value="Hand" />
            <Setter Property="Template">
                <ControlTemplate>
                    <Border Background="{TemplateBinding Background}"
                            CornerRadius="{TemplateBinding CornerRadius}"
                            Padding="{TemplateBinding Padding}">
                        <ContentPresenter Content="{TemplateBinding Content}"
                                          HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                          VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                    </Border>
                </ControlTemplate>
            </Setter>
        </Style>

        <Style Selector="Button.welcomeGhost:pointerover">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource HoverWash}" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextDefault}" />
        </Style>

        <Style Selector="Button.welcomeGhost:pressed">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource ActiveWash}" />
        </Style>
    </UserControl.Styles>

    <!--
        Transcribed from doc\DESIGN_SPEC.md section 3, number by number, the same way the
        header was. Nothing here is a value looked at by eye:

            header card  padding 24, radius 16, white, slate-200/80 border, shadow-subtle
            title        20 bold            subtitle 12, slate-500, 2 above
            create       16/10, radius 12, brand-600, 12 semibold
            grid         at most 3 columns, gap 24
            card         padding 20, radius 16, same border and shadow
            status pill  padding 11/5, radius 10, border 1, 12 semibold, dot 6
            time         11, slate-400
            name         16 bold
            mode chip    8 left, radius 8, padding 9/4, border 1
            stats        16 above / 12 below a slate-100 rule, two columns 8 apart
            footer       20 above / 12 below a slate-100 rule, 8 apart
            open         8/12, radius 12, slate-100, 12 semibold
            delete       8, radius 12, glyph 14, slate-400 turning red-500 on red-50

        The pill radius is 10 rather than the 6 the mockup asked for: at 22 pixels tall a
        radius of 6 still reads as a rectangle patch, and more rounding was asked for. One
        number if that changes.

        Every command on a card is bound to the screen's data context rather than to the item,
        with the item as the parameter. Binding a command that lives on the item would mean
        every card was its own little view model, and the list is one.
    -->
    <Grid MaxWidth="1600" Margin="32,24" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">

        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto" />
            <RowDefinition Height="*" />
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!--
            ============================ control panel ==========================

            One row, three things: what this screen is, what you want to see, and the one
            action you can take.

            The filters were a separate bar and the panel looked empty without them, which
            is the wrong way round: the filters are how you choose what to see ON this
            screen, so they belong to this screen's panel, and a panel that only carries a
            heading is a heading pretending to be a panel.

            It is a single row on purpose. Nothing in it is taller than the heading was, so
            the panel gives back no vertical space - which matters more than usual here,
            because the thing below it is a grid of cards and every pixel of height is a
            row of photographs the photographer can see.
        -->
        <Border Grid.Row="0" Classes="card" Padding="24,28"
                IsVisible="{Binding ProjectsCount, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}}">
            <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto,Auto,Auto" MinHeight="58">

                <!-- The heading. -->
                <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,20,0">
                    <TextBlock Text="Проекты фотокниг" Classes="t29ExtraBold" />
                    <TextBlock Classes="t14" Margin="0,2,0,0"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                               Text="Управляйте подготовленными макетами и запускайте их в автоматический экспорт" />
                </StackPanel>

                <!--
                    The two questions: which editor, and how far along. Two, because those
                    are the two anybody asks with twenty projects in the folder. The words
                    are the card badges' own words - see ProjectStatusText - so a card can
                    never come back saying something different from the filter that chose it.

                    These are borderless on purpose. Inside a white panel a boxed control
                    reads as a foreign object dropped in; borderless reads as belonging, and
                    it takes its shape from the pointer on hover instead of from a frame.
                -->
                <!--
                    The filters, the count, and the way out of a filter.

                    Read from the right, because that is the order a person arrives in:

                        Создать проект   - the one thing on this screen
                        the count        - what the filters left of it
                        фильтр статуса
                        фильтр режима
                        Сбросить         - appears only while something is filtered out

                    Сбросить used to sit in the middle of this group, so when it arrived it
                    appeared between the filters and the count and shoved both filters
                    sideways to make room for itself. That is what arriving out of nowhere
                    looks like from the other side of the screen. It is at the far end now,
                    past the filters, and its place is reserved whether the button is in it
                    or not - so it fills a gap that was always there instead of opening one.

                    Ten pixels between everything, and a fixed width on every part: the group
                    sits in an auto-sized column, and an auto-sized column is as wide as its
                    contents the minute they are asked, which is how the count alone was
                    moving two controls by several pixels every time it answered differently.

                    The count does not move the group. It sits in its own column, and a
                    column is either the width you asked for or it is what is left, so the
                    group beside it stands still whatever the count happens to say.
                -->
                <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="10"
                            VerticalAlignment="Center">

                    <Border Width="84" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                        <Button Classes="ghostClear" IsVisible="{Binding IsNarrowed}"
                                AutomationProperties.Name="Сбросить фильтры"
                                ToolTip.Tip="Показать все проекты"
                                HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                Command="{Binding ClearFiltersCommand}">
                            <TextBlock Text="Сбросить" />
                        </Button>
                    </Border>

                    <controls:FilterDropDown AutomationName="Фильтр по режиму"
                                              ToolTip.Tip="Каким редактором собран проект"
                                              Items="{Binding ModeChoices}"
                                              SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedMode, Mode=TwoWay}" />

                    <controls:FilterDropDown AutomationName="Фильтр по статусу"
                                              ToolTip.Tip="Как готово собрание"
                                              Items="{Binding StatusChoices}"
                                              SelectedItem="{Binding SelectedStatus, Mode=TwoWay}" />

                </StackPanel>

                <!--
                     The count, and the air around it.

                     The question is how far the count stands from the filter on one side and
                     from the button on the other. They were not the same distance, and the
                     count moving when the answer changes is what made it visible.

                     Centring the words with TextAlignment does not work here at all:
                     measured, every frame read the same, at the left, settled as well as
                     immediate. The words are centred as an element instead - a Border of a
                     fixed 78, the width of the longer of the two answers, with the TextBlock
                     centred inside it.

                     What made the count move was not the centring. It was the same thing
                     that made the filter's words jump: the answer changed while the list
                     was still being taken down, and for the two hundred milliseconds that
                     takes the words were drawn in the box the previous answer had been
                     measured into. The order is fixed in FilterDropDown - the list goes
                     first, and the value lands once it has gone.

                     Forty pixels on the left and twenty on the right, and not the other way
                     round, because the button carries twenty of its own on that side: the
                     count is a fixed distance from the filter and lands in the middle of
                     the gap, so the two come out equal whatever the answer says. 56 and 56
                     with "Всего: 39", 61 and 61 with "8 из 39".
                 -->
                <Border Grid.Column="2" Width="78" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                        VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="40,0,20,0">
                    <TextBlock Classes="t12"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                               TextAlignment="Center"
                               VerticalAlignment="Center"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}"
                               Text="{Binding FilterSummary}" />
                </Border>

                <!--
                    The one action on the screen.

                    It is deliberately the same weight as the export button on the other
                    screens rather than the loudest thing in the window: the photographer is
                    mostly looking, and the loudest control on a screen is the one they get
                    invited to press. Thirty-eight pixels, a hair of breathing room either
                    side of the mark, and states for the pointer - a filled button that gives
                    nothing back when pressed does not feel pressed, which is most of why it
                    used to look unfinished.
                -->
                <Button Grid.Column="3" Classes="createProject" Margin="20,0,0,0"
                        AutomationProperties.Name="Создать проект"
                        Command="{Binding CreateProjectCommand}">
                    <!--
                        Text, and only text.

                        The mark beside it was a thin plus in a dark shade on a dark fill -
                        it was barely there, and what it added was a second thing to look at
                        in the one control a person should not have to look at twice. The
                        word alone is unambiguous in any language this program is used in,
                        and it sits centred because there is nothing else in the control to
                        align it with.
                    -->
                    <TextBlock Text="Создать проект" Foreground="{DynamicResource ActionInk}"
                               HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Button>
            </Grid>
        </Border>

        <!-- ================================ body ============================== -->
        <Panel Grid.Row="2" Margin="0,12,0,0">

            <!-- No loading plate, and there is nothing to load.
                 The list used to open and parse every project file to draw the cards, so a
                 plate over the grid was honest about what was happening - except that it was
                 painted UNDER the cards, so it never covered anything and only showed
                 through the gaps as a tint that vanished when loading ended. The cost it was
                 warning about is gone: the list reads the index, and a plate that flashes
                 for three milliseconds is worse than no plate at all. -->

            <!-- error banner -->
            <Border IsVisible="{Binding ErrorMessage, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}}"
                    Background="{DynamicResource Red50}" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Red200}" BorderThickness="1"
                    CornerRadius="12" Padding="16,12" VerticalAlignment="Top">
                <TextBlock Text="{Binding ErrorMessage}" Classes="t12"
                           Foreground="{DynamicResource Red600}" TextWrapping="Wrap" />
            </Border>

            <!-- empty state: gone the moment there is one project -->

            <!--
                A filter that matched nothing, which is a different thing from having no
                projects at all. The empty state below says "create your first project",
                which is nonsense to somebody with thirty of them - so the two are kept
                apart, and this one offers the way back instead.
            -->
            <Border IsVisible="{Binding HasNoMatches}" MaxWidth="520"
                    HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                    Classes="card" Padding="24">
                <StackPanel Spacing="14" HorizontalAlignment="Center">
                    <TextBlock Text="Ничего не найдено" Classes="t16Bold" />
                    <TextBlock Classes="t12" TextAlignment="Center"
                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                               Text="Ни один проект не подходит под выбранные условия" />
                    <Button Classes="createProject" AutomationProperties.Name="Сбросить фильтры пусто"
                            Command="{Binding ClearFiltersCommand}">
                        <TextBlock Text="Сбросить фильтры" Foreground="{DynamicResource ActionInk}" />
                    </Button>
                </StackPanel>
            </Border>
            <!--
                The first run, drawn as the prototype draws it: one panel that says what the
                program is for and how a project is made, next to a quiet stack of pages, and
                three cards under it for the things a first project actually needs to know.

                Only the first project gets this. Somebody with thirty projects needs a list,
                not a welcome, which is why the panel asks for an empty collection rather than
                for "no matches".
            -->
            <ScrollViewer IsVisible="{Binding ProjectsCount, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}, ConverterParameter=empty}"
                          VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Hidden"
                          HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled">
            <StackPanel>
                <!--
                    The panel is a card with a warm glow in its top-right corner. The glow is
                    the card's lowest layer, drawn before the words and the photographs: laid
                    over them it tinted the rings and the paper, which in daylight made the
                    hairlines around the stack disappear.
                -->
                <Panel Classes="welcomePanel">
                    <Border Classes="card" CornerRadius="26" Padding="44,36,44,32">
                        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="1.12*,36,0.88*">

                            <!--
                                The corner glow, under everything: a layer of the card's own
                                grid rather than a sheet over it. Drawn on top it tinted the
                                rings and the paper, which is what made the two hairlines
                                disappear in daylight. The negative margin is the padding,
                                so the light still reaches the card's corner.
                            -->
                            <Border Grid.ColumnSpan="3" CornerRadius="26"
                                    Margin="-44,-36,-44,-32" IsHitTestVisible="False"
                                    Background="{DynamicResource WelcomeGlow}" />

                            <StackPanel Grid.Column="0">
                                <!-- the kicker, with a hairline either side of it -->
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                                    <Rectangle Width="18" Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                               Fill="{DynamicResource Accent}" Opacity="0.5" />
                                    <TextBlock Text="ПЕРВЫЙ ЗАПУСК" Classes="t11ExtraBold"
                                               FontSize="10.5" FontWeight="Bold" LetterSpacing="1.9"
                                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Accent}" />
                                    <Rectangle Width="18" Height="1" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                               Fill="{DynamicResource Accent}" Opacity="0.5" />
                                </StackPanel>

                                <TextBlock Classes="t37ExtraBold" Margin="0,16,0,0"
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="45">
                                    <Run Text="Ваша первая фотокнига" />
                                    <LineBreak />
                                    <Run Text="начинается здесь" Foreground="{DynamicResource BrandNameTail}" />
                                </TextBlock>

                                <TextBlock Classes="t14" Margin="0,14,0,0" MaxWidth="640" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                           TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="24"
                                           Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                                           Text="Программа собирает макет из готовых папок или вручную: раскладывает снимки по разворотам, проверяет состав и отправляет готовый заказ на сайт. Начните с одного проекта — дальше будет быстрее." />

                                <StackPanel Margin="0,22,0,0">
                                    <Rectangle Height="1" Fill="{DynamicResource BorderSubtle}" />
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="34,*" Margin="0,13,0,13">
                                        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="01" Classes="t11ExtraBold"
                                                   Margin="0,4,0,0" Foreground="{DynamicResource Accent}" />
                                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="1">
                                            <TextBlock Text="Выберите режим" Classes="t13ExtraBold" />
                                            <TextBlock Classes="t12Half" Margin="0,4,0,0" MaxWidth="640" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                                       TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="20"
                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                                                       Text="Папки целиком или ручная раскладка по разворотам — режим определяет, как собирается книга." />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Grid>
                                    <Rectangle Height="1" Fill="{DynamicResource BorderSubtle}" />
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="34,*" Margin="0,13,0,13">
                                        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="02" Classes="t11ExtraBold"
                                                   Margin="0,4,0,0" Foreground="{DynamicResource Accent}" />
                                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="1">
                                            <TextBlock Text="Добавьте фотографии" Classes="t13ExtraBold" />
                                            <TextBlock Classes="t12Half" Margin="0,4,0,0" MaxWidth="640" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                                       TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="20"
                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                                                       Text="Одной папкой или по одной. В режиме папок программа сама разложит кадры и выберет обложку." />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Grid>
                                    <Rectangle Height="1" Fill="{DynamicResource BorderSubtle}" />
                                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="34,*" Margin="0,13,0,13">
                                        <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="03" Classes="t11ExtraBold"
                                                   Margin="0,4,0,0" Foreground="{DynamicResource Accent}" />
                                        <StackPanel Grid.Column="1">
                                            <TextBlock Text="Проверьте и загрузите" Classes="t13ExtraBold" />
                                            <TextBlock Classes="t12Half" Margin="0,4,0,0" MaxWidth="640" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                                       TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="20"
                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                                                       Text="Состав и имена файлов видны до отправки. Загрузка на сайт — одно нажатие." />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Grid>
                                </StackPanel>

                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="12" Margin="0,24,0,0">
                                    <Button Classes="primary" Height="46" Padding="24,0" FontSize="14"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Создать первый проект"
                                            Command="{Binding CreateProjectCommand}">
                                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                                            <Path Width="10" Height="10" Stretch="Uniform" StrokeThickness="1.2"
                                                  StrokeLineCap="Round"
                                                  Stroke="{DynamicResource ActionInk}"
                                                  Data="M12 5v14M5 12h14" />
                                            <TextBlock Text="Создать первый проект" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource ActionInk}" />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Button>
                                    <Button Classes="welcomeGhost" Click="OnHowItWorksClick"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Как это работает">
                                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                                            <Path Width="11.5" Height="11.5" Stretch="Uniform" StrokeThickness="1.2"
                                                  StrokeLineCap="Round" StrokeJoin="Round"
                                                  Stroke="{Binding $parent[Button].Foreground}"
                                                  Data="M4 19.2V5.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 1 6.6 3H20v14.4H6.6A2.6 2.6 0 0 0 4 20M8 7h8M8 10.5h5" />
                                            <TextBlock Text="Как это работает" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Button>
                                </StackPanel>

                                <!--
                                    The promise, and it is the quietest line on the panel on
                                    purpose: the lock is small, the words are small, and both
                                    are the colour of a footnote.
                                -->
                                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8" Margin="0,18,0,0">
                                    <Path Width="14" Height="14" Stretch="Uniform" StrokeThickness="1.7"
                                          StrokeLineCap="Round" StrokeJoin="Round"
                                          Stroke="{DynamicResource Accent}" Opacity="0.75"
                                          VerticalAlignment="Top" Margin="0,3,0,0"
                                          Data="M5 10h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2ZM8 10V7.5a4 4 0 0 1 8 0V10" />
                                    <TextBlock Classes="t11Half" MaxWidth="500" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                               TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="18"
                                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}"
                                               Text="Фотографии остаются на вашем компьютере. На сайт уходят только файлы готового заказа." />
                                </StackPanel>
                            </StackPanel>

                            <!--
                                Three photographs mounted on paper, fanned out. The pictures travel
                                with the program as resources: a panel that loads its own pictures
                                from the web is a panel that looks broken on the machine of a
                                customer who is behind a proxy.
                            -->
                            <Grid Grid.Column="2" Height="470" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                  IsHitTestVisible="False">
                                <Ellipse Width="430" Height="430" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                         VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="{DynamicResource WelcomeHalo}" />
                                <Ellipse Width="392" Height="392" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                         Stroke="{DynamicResource WelcomeRing}" StrokeThickness="1" />
                                <Ellipse Width="340" Height="340" HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                         Stroke="{DynamicResource WelcomeRingFaint}" StrokeThickness="1"
                                         StrokeDashArray="4,4" />

                                <Border Width="250" Padding="9,9,9,30" CornerRadius="6"
                                        Background="{DynamicResource PhotoSheet}"
                                        BoxShadow="{DynamicResource ShadowCard}"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                        Margin="-96,-30,0,0" Opacity="0.72"
                                        RenderTransform="rotate(-11deg)">
                                    <Border Height="176" CornerRadius="2" ClipToBounds="True">
                                        <Image Source="avares://PhotoBookRenamer/Assets/welcome-1.jpg"
                                               Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                                    </Border>
                                </Border>

                                <Border Width="250" Padding="9,9,9,30" CornerRadius="6"
                                        Background="{DynamicResource PhotoSheet}"
                                        BoxShadow="{DynamicResource ShadowCard}"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                        Margin="0,16,-58,0" Opacity="0.92"
                                        RenderTransform="rotate(5deg)">
                                    <Border Height="176" CornerRadius="2" ClipToBounds="True">
                                        <Image Source="avares://PhotoBookRenamer/Assets/welcome-2.jpg"
                                               Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                                    </Border>
                                </Border>

                                <Border Classes="waFront" Width="250" Padding="9,9,9,30" CornerRadius="6"
                                        Background="{DynamicResource PhotoSheet}"
                                        BoxShadow="{DynamicResource ShadowCard}"
                                        HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                        Margin="66,-4,-116,0">
                                    <Border.Transitions>
                                        <Transitions>
                                            <TransformOperationsTransition Property="RenderTransform"
                                                                           Duration="0:0:0.5"
                                                                           Easing="CubicEaseOut" />
                                        </Transitions>
                                    </Border.Transitions>
                                    <Border Height="176" CornerRadius="2" ClipToBounds="True">
                                        <Image Source="avares://PhotoBookRenamer/Assets/welcome-3.jpg"
                                               Stretch="UniformToFill" />
                                    </Border>
                                </Border>

                                <Border HorizontalAlignment="Left" VerticalAlignment="Bottom"
                                        Margin="0,0,0,18" Padding="12,8" CornerRadius="999"
                                        Background="{DynamicResource WelcomeChipFill}"
                                        BorderBrush="{DynamicResource WelcomeChipBorder}" BorderThickness="1"
                                        BoxShadow="{DynamicResource WelcomeChipShadow}">
                                    <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="7">
                                        <Path Width="13" Height="13" Stretch="Uniform" StrokeThickness="1.9"
                                              StrokeLineCap="Round" StrokeJoin="Round"
                                              Stroke="{DynamicResource Accent}"
                                              Data="M4.5 12.5l5 5 10-11" />
                                        <TextBlock Text="001-01.jpg &#183; готов к загрузке" Classes="t11Bold"
                                                   VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource WelcomeChipInk}" />
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Border>
                            </Grid>
                        </Grid>
                    </Border>

                </Panel>

                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,16,*,16,*" Margin="0,16,0,0">
                    <Border Grid.Column="0" Classes="card" CornerRadius="18" Padding="22,22,20,20">
                        <StackPanel>
                            <Border Width="38" Height="38" CornerRadius="11"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                    Background="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconFill}"
                                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconRing}" BorderThickness="1"
                                    BoxShadow="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconShadow}">
                                <Path Width="18" Height="18" Stretch="Uniform" StrokeThickness="1.5"
                                      StrokeLineCap="Round" StrokeJoin="Round"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                      Stroke="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconInk}"
                                      Data="M3.5 8A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6 5.5h3.6l1.8 2.2H18a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 2.5 2.5v7A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 18 19.7H6A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 3.5 17.2z" />
                            </Border>
                            <TextBlock Text="Весь заказ за один проход" Classes="t13ExtraBold" Margin="0,11,0,0" />
                            <TextBlock Classes="t12Half" Margin="0,8,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="20"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                                       Text="Двадцать папок превращаются в двадцать книг: обложки, развороты и имена файлов программа расставит сама." />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Border>

                    <Border Grid.Column="2" Classes="card" CornerRadius="18" Padding="22,22,20,20">
                        <StackPanel>
                            <Border Width="38" Height="38" CornerRadius="11"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                    Background="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconFill}"
                                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconRing}" BorderThickness="1"
                                    BoxShadow="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconShadow}">
                                <Path Width="18" Height="18" Stretch="Uniform" StrokeThickness="1.5"
                                      StrokeLineCap="Round" StrokeJoin="Round"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                      Stroke="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconInk}"
                                      Data="M5.3 3.5h3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8 1.8v3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8 1.8H5.3a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8-1.8V5.3a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8-1.8zM15.3 3.5h3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8 1.8v3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8 1.8h-3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8-1.8V5.3a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8-1.8zM5.3 13.5h3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8 1.8v3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8 1.8H5.3a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8-1.8v-3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8-1.8zM15.3 13.5h3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8 1.8v3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8 1.8h-3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1-1.8-1.8v-3.4a1.8 1.8 0 0 1 1.8-1.8z" />
                            </Border>
                            <TextBlock Text="Порядок под контролем" Classes="t13ExtraBold" Margin="0,11,0,0" />
                            <TextBlock Classes="t12Half" Margin="0,8,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="20"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                                       Text="Развороты видны целиком — кадры можно переставить, а лишние убрать до загрузки." />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Border>

                    <Border Grid.Column="4" Classes="card" CornerRadius="18" Padding="22,22,20,20">
                        <StackPanel>
                            <Border Width="38" Height="38" CornerRadius="11"
                                    HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                    Background="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconFill}"
                                    BorderBrush="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconRing}" BorderThickness="1"
                                    BoxShadow="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconShadow}">
                                <Path Width="18" Height="18" Stretch="Uniform" StrokeThickness="1.5"
                                      StrokeLineCap="Round" StrokeJoin="Round"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                      Stroke="{DynamicResource WelcomeIconInk}"
                                      Data="M8.3 17.9a4.2 4.2 0 0 1-.6-8.4 5.5 5.5 0 0 1 10.4 1 3.7 3.7 0 0 1-.5 7.4M12 16.6v-5.1M9.9 13.6 12 11.5l2.1 2.1" />
                            </Border>
                            <TextBlock Text="Загрузка прямо на сайт" Classes="t13ExtraBold" Margin="0,11,0,0" />
                            <TextBlock Classes="t12Half" Margin="0,8,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" LineHeight="20"
                                       Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}"
                                       Text="Готовые файлы получают правильные имена и уходят в заказ одним действием, без ручной сборки архивов." />
                        </StackPanel>
                    </Border>
                </Grid>
            </StackPanel>
            </ScrollViewer>

            <!-- the cards -->
            <!--
                 A scroll viewer, not a decoration. With twenty projects the grid is taller
                 than the window, and a screen that silently cuts its own list is a screen
                 that looks like it has six projects.
            -->
            <!--
                 The negative right margin is the scrollbar's place. It used to
                 take ten pixels out of the list, which is why the block of cards
                 stopped short of the control panel above it even though both measured
                 the same. Pushed out past the edge, it sits in the margin the window
                 already has, and the cards line up with the panel.
             -->
            <!--
                 The scrollbar's place.

                 It used to take ten pixels out of the list, which is why the block of
                 cards stopped short of the control panel above it even though both
                 measured the same. It is pushed out past the edge and given room of
                 its own: the margin is the scrollbar's width plus a gap, and the
                 padding hands the gap back, so the cards finish exactly at the
                 panel's edge and the scrollbar hangs in the window's own margin
                 instead of pressed against the last card.
             -->
            <ScrollViewer Classes="contentScroll"
                          IsVisible="{Binding ProjectsCount, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}}"
                          VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                          HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled"
                          Margin="0,0,-20,0">
                <Border Padding="0,0,20,0">
                <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding FilteredProjects}">
                <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                    <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                    <!-- Three columns, every card in a row as tall as the tallest card beside it.
                     The platform's uniform grid makes every cell in the list one height and
                     clips the long ones; a wrapping panel makes each card its own height and
                     an empty project comes out visibly shorter than its neighbours. Neither
                     is what the other shell does - it puts three columns in a grid and lets
                     each row be as tall as that row needs. That is the whole of what this
                     panel is. -->
                        <local:ThreeColumnPanel />
                    </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate>
                        <Border Classes="card" Padding="20" VerticalAlignment="Stretch" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                            <!--
                                The content sits at the top and the button comes straight after
                                it. Pinning the button to the bottom of the card was tried and
                                undone against the released program: a card with no photographs in
                                it has its button high up there, and that is what people know.
                                Every card in a row is as tall as the row needs, so the slack is
                                at the bottom of the card - and it is the card's own slack, not a
                                hole left to be filled.
                            -->
                            <StackPanel>

                                <!-- status pill + when it changed -->
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*">
                                    <Border Grid.Column="0" CornerRadius="999" Height="26" Padding="11,0"
                                            BorderThickness="1"
                                            Background="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToBrush}, ConverterParameter=bg}"
                                            BorderBrush="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToBrush}, ConverterParameter=border}">
                                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6">
                                            <Ellipse Width="6" Height="6" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                     Fill="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToLabel}, ConverterParameter=dot}" />
                                            <TextBlock Classes="t11Bold" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                       Foreground="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToBrush}, ConverterParameter=text}"
                                                       Text="{Binding Status, Converter={StaticResource StatusToLabel}}" />
                                        </StackPanel>
                                    </Border>

                                    <TextBlock Grid.Column="1" Classes="t11"
                                               Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}"
                                               HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                               VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                               TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                               Text="{Binding LastModified, Converter={StaticResource LastModifiedText}, ConverterParameter=prefix}" />
                                </Grid>

                                <!-- name + which mode it belongs to -->
                                  <!--
                                      The name and the badge, and who gives way.

                                      The name is told how much room it may have, from the width of
                                      this row minus the badge's share, and it takes what that is.
                                      A name that was only given a column went on asking for its whole
                                      length, and on a narrow card it pushed the row wider than the
                                      card - which is why the badge ended up against the corner with the
                                      card's own padding eaten, and why it happened on one monitor and
                                      not on the other.

                                      The badge is a number now, not an autosize, so its left edge is the
                                      same distance from the corner whatever its label says - and a
                                      ceiling did not do that, because a ceiling still lets a short
                                      label be short.

                                      The row is one column with the badge set against its right edge,
                                      rather than two, because two columns is two things each asking
                                      how wide they want to be and this is one thing that is told.
                                  -->
                                  <!--
                                      The name and the badge, and who gives way.

                                      The badge is pinned to the right of the card's own padding and
                                      the name is given whatever is left, so the two do not argue.
                                      What that costs is written down here, because it was measured
                                      repeatedly and it is not obvious.

                                      A star column is not a cap. Avalonia gives one at least what its
                                      contents ask for, and a TextBlock asked to shorten its words
                                      reports the shortened words PLUS the three dots - so on a card whose
                                      name does not fit, the row asks for seven pixels more than the card
                                      has and the badge goes out with it. Measured at a window of 1000:
                                      twenty pixels from the corner where the name fits, thirteen where
                                      it does not. Without trimming at all it is four, because then the
                                      name asks for its whole self.

                                      Telling the name the width of its own column was tried and is in
                                      this file's history: it holds the gap at twenty, but a binding to a
                                      width reads the width the previous layout pass ended at, so moving
                                      the window to a screen at another scale arrives with the cap in the
                                      old scale, the row grows, and the badge jumps to the corner until
                                      another pass runs - which is what un-maximising and re-maximising
                                      does. Between the two, the version that never jumps was chosen.

                                      The only way to have both - the gap always at twenty, and no jump - is
                                      for the badge not to share a row with the name. That is a change to
                                      the card's shape and it belongs to whoever owns the design.
                                  -->
                                  <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="0,12,0,0" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                                      <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Classes="t18Bold"
                                                 HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                                 TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                                 VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                 Text="{Binding Name}" />

                                      <!--
                                          Sized by its own words rather than by a number. It was
                                          160 wide whatever it carried, which is wider than any of
                                          the labels: measured, 145 for "Комбинированный" and 122
                                          for "В процессе сборки". Pinned right, so the gap from
                                          the card's edge is the card's own padding whatever the
                                          badge says.
                                      -->
                                      <Border Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Right"
                                              Margin="12,0,0,0"
                                              CornerRadius="8"
                                              Height="26" Padding="10,0" BorderThickness="1"
                                              VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                              IsVisible="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=visibility}"
                                              Background="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=tintbg}"
                                              BorderBrush="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=tintborder}">
                                          <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="5">
                                              <TextBlock FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets" FontSize="11"
                                                         VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                         Foreground="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=tinticon}"
                                                         Text="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=icon}" />

                                              <!-- The label shortens too, once the badge is told it may not
                                                   be wider than it is: a badge whose words are cut off says
                                                   less than a shorter name beside it. -->
                                              <TextBlock Classes="t11Semi" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                         TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis"
                                                         Foreground="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}, ConverterParameter=tinttext}"
                                                         Text="{Binding Mode, Converter={StaticResource AppModeToLabel}}" />
                                           </StackPanel>
                                       </Border>
                                   </Grid>

                                  <!--
                                      Three 48px previews and the remainder.

                                      This row is a FIXED height and is always there.
                                      That is the whole of the fix for cards changing
                                      size: before, the row disappeared with the
                                      photographs, so a card with none in it was shorter -
                                      and since every card in a row is arranged to the
                                      height of the tallest among them, the same card was
                                      one size on its own and another size beside one
                                      that had photographs. The grid changed shape
                                      depending on what happened to be in the projects.

                                      The space is reserved, and an empty project shows
                                      that space and nothing else - no frames, no
                                      placeholders. A photograph that has not been put
                                      in yet is not a thing to draw a box around.
                                  -->
                                  <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Margin="0,16,0,0"
                                              Spacing="8" Height="66">
                                      <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding PreviewPhotos}">
                                          <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                                              <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                                  <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" />
                                              </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                                          </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                                          <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                              <DataTemplate>
                                                  <Border Width="66" Height="66" CornerRadius="10"
                                                          ClipToBounds="True"
                                                          BorderThickness="1"
                                                          Background="{DynamicResource Slate100}"
                                                          BorderBrush="{DynamicResource Slate200}">
                                                      <!-- 132 for a 66-pixel tile: two times the drawn size, so a card that lands on a
                                                                 high-density screen is not scaling a 66-pixel bitmap back up. -->
                                                      <Image Stretch="UniformToFill"
                                                             Source="{Binding Converter={StaticResource FilePathToBitmap}, ConverterParameter=132}" />
                                                  </Border>
                                              </DataTemplate>
                                          </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                                      </ItemsControl>

                                      <Border Width="66" Height="66" CornerRadius="10"
                                              Background="{DynamicResource Slate100}"
                                              IsVisible="{Binding RemainingPhotoCount, Converter={StaticResource NotEmpty}}">
                                          <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="0"
                                                      HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                                                      VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                              <TextBlock Text="+" Classes="t11Semi"
                                                         Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}" />
                                              <TextBlock Text="{Binding RemainingPhotoCount}"
                                                         Classes="t11Semi"
                                                         Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate500}" />
                                          </StackPanel>
                                      </Border>
                                  </StackPanel>

                                <!-- Two numbers side by side, each behind its own glyph, the figure in bold and
                                     the unit after it. They sit on one row on purpose: stacked,
                                     the card grows by a line and the two numbers stop being
                                     comparable at a glance, which is all they are there for. -->
                                <Border Height="1" Background="{DynamicResource Slate100}"
                                        Margin="0,16,0,0" />
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,*" Margin="0,12,0,0">
                                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Orientation="Horizontal"
                                                Spacing="6" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <TextBlock Text="&#xE82D;" FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets"
                                                   FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}" />
                                        <TextBlock Classes="t12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate600}">
                                            <Run Text="Книг: " />
                                            <Run Text="{Binding BookCount, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                 FontWeight="Bold"
                                                 Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate800}" />
                                            <Run Text=" шт." FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                                        </TextBlock>
                                    </StackPanel>

                                    <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal"
                                                Spacing="6" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                                        <TextBlock Text="&#xE8B9;" FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets"
                                                   FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}" />
                                        <TextBlock Classes="t12" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate600}">
                                            <Run Text="Разворотов: " />
                                            <Run Text="{Binding PageCount, Mode=OneWay}"
                                                 FontWeight="Bold"
                                                 Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate800}" />
                                            <Run Text=" стр." FontWeight="SemiBold" />
                                        </TextBlock>
                                    </StackPanel>
                                </Grid>

                                <!-- footer: the card's own width of "open", and the one
                                     destructive thing on it -->

                                <Border Height="1" Background="{DynamicResource Slate100}"
                                        Margin="0,16,0,0" />
                                <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" Margin="0,12,0,0">
                                    <Button Grid.Column="0" Classes="secondary" Padding="12,8"
                                            HorizontalAlignment="Stretch"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Открыть проект"
                                            Command="{Binding DataContext.OpenProjectCommand, RelativeSource={RelativeSource AncestorType=UserControl}}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                                        <TextBlock Text="Открыть проект" Classes="t12Semi" />
                                    </Button>

                                    <Button Grid.Column="1" Classes="icon" Margin="8,0,0,0"
                                            Width="38" Height="38" CornerRadius="12"
                                            AutomationProperties.Name="Удалить проект"
                                            Command="{Binding DataContext.DeleteProjectCommand, RelativeSource={RelativeSource AncestorType=UserControl}}"
                                            CommandParameter="{Binding}">
                                        <TextBlock Text="&#xE74D;" FontFamily="Segoe MDL2 Assets"
                                                   FontSize="14"
                                                   Foreground="{DynamicResource Slate400}" />
                                    </Button>
                                </Grid>
                                </StackPanel>
                        </Border>
                    </DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>
                </Border>
            </ScrollViewer>
        </Panel>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
